  "notes": {
    "raw": "Phase change: 505.12 K, melting point of Sn; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 1.680$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n$$\n\\begin{array}{r l} 2 9 8. 1 5 - 6 5 0 \\mathrm{K}: & \\mathrm{Cp} ^ {\\circ} = 2 8. 9 0 0 + 4. 1 7 2 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} - 1. 6 2 1 \\times 1 0 ^ {5} \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 2} \\\\ & \\mathrm{H} ^ {\\circ} - \\mathrm{H} _ {2 9 8} ^ {\\circ} = 2 8. 9 0 0 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} + 2. 0 8 6 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 1. 6 2 1 \\times 1 0 ^ {2} \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} - 9. 3 4 6 \\end{array}\n$$\nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n$$\n\\begin{array}{l} 2 9 8. 1 5 - 5 0 5. 1 2 \\mathrm{K}: \\Delta \\mathrm{Hr} ^ {\\circ} = - 1 0 8. 7 6 5 + 6. 4 4 9 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} - 3. 0 7 8 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 7 4. 8 5 0 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} \\\\ \\Delta G r ^ {\\circ} = - 1 0 8. 7 6 5 - 6. 4 4 9 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{TlnT} + 3. 0 7 8 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 3 7. 4 2 5 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} + 1 0 8. 9 1 3 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} \\\\ 5 0 5. 1 2 - 6 5 0 \\mathrm{K}: \\quad \\Delta \\mathrm{Hr} ^ {\\circ} = - 1 1 2. 6 9 7 + 4. 0 0 3 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} + 1. 2 4 4 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 4 3 0. 4 5 0 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} \\\\ \\Delta G r ^ {\\circ} = - 1 1 2. 6 9 7 - 4. 0 0 3 x 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{TlnT} - 1. 2 4 4 x 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 2 1 5. 2 2 5 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} + 1 0 2. 9 5 6 x 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} \\\\ \\end{array}\n$$\nSources: Enthalpy of formation at 298 K from Wiedemeier (130). Other data from Wiedemeier (131) who extrapolated heat capacities 0-110 K to derive entropy at 298 K. ",
    "lines_raw": [
      "Phase change: 505.12 K, melting point of Sn; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 1.680$ kcal/mol.",
      "Heat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations:",
      "$$",
      "\\begin{array}{r l} 2 9 8. 1 5 - 6 5 0 \\mathrm{K}: & \\mathrm{Cp} ^ {\\circ} = 2 8. 9 0 0 + 4. 1 7 2 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} - 1. 6 2 1 \\times 1 0 ^ {5} \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 2} \\\\ & \\mathrm{H} ^ {\\circ} - \\mathrm{H} _ {2 9 8} ^ {\\circ} = 2 8. 9 0 0 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} + 2. 0 8 6 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 1. 6 2 1 \\times 1 0 ^ {2} \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} - 9. 3 4 6 \\end{array}",
      "$$",
      "Reaction equations (kcal/mol):",
      "$$",
      "\\begin{array}{l} 2 9 8. 1 5 - 5 0 5. 1 2 \\mathrm{K}: \\Delta \\mathrm{Hr} ^ {\\circ} = - 1 0 8. 7 6 5 + 6. 4 4 9 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} - 3. 0 7 8 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 7 4. 8 5 0 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} \\\\ \\Delta G r ^ {\\circ} = - 1 0 8. 7 6 5 - 6. 4 4 9 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{TlnT} + 3. 0 7 8 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 3 7. 4 2 5 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} + 1 0 8. 9 1 3 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} \\\\ 5 0 5. 1 2 - 6 5 0 \\mathrm{K}: \\quad \\Delta \\mathrm{Hr} ^ {\\circ} = - 1 1 2. 6 9 7 + 4. 0 0 3 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} + 1. 2 4 4 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 4 3 0. 4 5 0 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} \\\\ \\Delta G r ^ {\\circ} = - 1 1 2. 6 9 7 - 4. 0 0 3 x 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{TlnT} - 1. 2 4 4 x 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 2 1 5. 2 2 5 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} + 1 0 2. 9 5 6 x 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} \\\\ \\end{array}",
      "$$",
      "Sources: Enthalpy of formation at 298 K from Wiedemeier (130). Other data from Wiedemeier (131) who extrapolated heat capacities 0-110 K to derive entropy at 298 K."
    ],
